Rule 2 (tensor dimensions must be at least 3 for cross product)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (tensor elements must be valid for cross product)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 3 ∧ shape(v_1, i) ≤ 3
>>
Rule 6 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 8 (tensor must have valid type for cross product)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 9 (tensor must be compatible with cross product)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) = 3
